.\" man page for mkslug
.TH MKSLUG 1 "2026-07-26" "mkslug 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mkslug \- slugify and unslugify text, files, and directories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mkslug
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ text " | " file-or-directory ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mkslug
converts text into URL\-, branch\-, and filename\-friendly
.IR slugs ,
and can convert slugs back into readable text.  Non\-ASCII input is romanized
with ICU (for example
.IR caf\('e "  becomes  " cafe ", " Z\(:urich " becomes " zurich ),"
so slugs are always safe ASCII.
.PP
If no positional argument is given, text is read from standard input.  In text
mode the resulting slug is printed to standard output and copied to the system
clipboard (unless disabled).  If the positional argument names an existing file
or directory (or
.B \-f
is given), mkslug operates in file mode instead: it previews or performs a
rename, preserving file extensions.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Common options
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show detailed help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIfile\fR
Override the configuration file.  By default
.I ~/.config/mkslug/default.conf
and
.I ~/.mkslug.conf
are read if present.
.TP
.BR \-U ", " \-\-unslug
Unslug the text/file/directory.  Case is preserved by default in this mode.
.SS Case-conversion options
These are mutually exclusive; the first one given wins.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-no\-change
Do not convert the case.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-lower
Convert to lowercase (the default in slug mode).
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-upper
Convert to uppercase.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-title
Convert to title case.
.SS Text-mode options
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-clipboard
Do not copy the result to the clipboard.  By default the slug is copied.
.SS File/directory-mode options
Unless
.B \-f
is given, mkslug checks whether the path exists and falls back to text mode if
it does not.  File extensions are preserved and never slugified.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Force file/directory mode even if the path does not exist.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-rename
Rename the entry on disk to its slug.
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-recurse
Recurse into directories.
.TP
.BR \-X ", " \-\-exclude " " \fIpat\fR
Comma\-separated patterns to exclude during recursion.
.TP
.BR \-I ", " \-\-include " " \fIpat\fR
Comma\-separated patterns to include during recursion.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-max\-depth " " \fIn\fR
Maximum recursion depth (0 means unlimited; the default).
.PP
In recursion with rename, files are renamed first and directories are renamed
from the bottom up, avoiding path\-traversal races.
.SH PATTERNS
Patterns for
.B \-X
and
.B \-I
are comma\-separated.  Each element is either a glob delimited by
.RB ' @ '
(for example
.BR @*.tmp@,@*.exe@ )
or an extended regular expression delimited by
.RB ' / '
(for example
.BR /^.+\e.(doc|ppt|xls)x?$/ ).
A regex may carry trailing flags after the closing slash:
.BR i " (case-insensitive), " m " (multiline), " s " (dot-all), " x
(extended), for example
.BR /^readme$/i .
A comma inside an element may be escaped with a backslash.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file uses simple
.I key = value
lines.  Recognized keys:
.BR separator ,
.BR case ,
.BR clipboard ,
.BR transliterate ,
and
.BR collapse .
Lines starting with
.RB ' # '
or
.RB ' ; '
are comments.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime error (I/O or encoding failure).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (bad command line).
.TP
.B 3
A required path did not exist.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B mkslug "Hello, World!"
Prints
.I hello-world
and copies it to the clipboard.
.TP
.B mkslug \-t "my cool post"
Prints
.IR My-Cool-Post .
.TP
.B mkslug \-U hello-world
Prints
.IR "hello world" .
.TP
.B mkslug \-r "My R\('esum\('e.PDF"
Renames the file to
.IR my-resume.PDF .
.TP
.B mkslug \-Rr \-X '@*.git@' ./docs
Recursively slug\-renames entries under
.IR ./docs .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mkslug/default.conf
.TQ
.I ~/.mkslug.conf
Default configuration files.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR iconv (1),
.BR pcre2 (3)
.SH AUTHORS
The mkslug contributors.
